    {
      "id": "p0168-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In some English-speaking regions, children are taught the phrase \"stop, drop, and roll\" as a way to remember what to do if their clothes catch on fire. This reference and Papyrus' fire puns would be lost in a literal translation, so the translator adjusted the line:",
        "raw": "In some English-speaking regions,\nchildren are taught the phrase \"stop,\ndrop, and roll\" as a way to remember\nwhat to do if their clothes catch on fire.\nThis reference and Papyrus' fire puns\nwould be lost in a literal translation, so\nthe translator adjusted the line:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.61120183,
          0.33105,
          0.90828152,
          0.45253571
        ],
