    {
      "id": "p0168-b012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "After some brainstorming, the localization team chose a new name for \"Sea Tea\": Bichabi-cha. This is a play on the Japanese words cha (\"tea\") and bichabicha (\"sopping wet; soggy\"), and was intended to sound like real-life tea brands such as Sokenbicha. Thus, the Japanese name for \"Sea Tea\" has a level of wordplay that goes beyond the simple rhyme of the original English name.",
        "raw": "After some brainstorming, the localization team chose a new name for \"Sea\nTea\": Bichabi-cha. This is a play on the Japanese words cha (\"tea\") and\nbichabicha (\"sopping wet; soggy\"), and was intended to sound like real-life tea\nbrands such as Sokenbicha. Thus, the Japanese name for \"Sea Tea\" has a level\nof wordplay that goes beyond the simple rhyme of the original English name.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29284458,
          0.81671429,
          0.89645385,
          0.90272143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2892524,
          0.816,
          0.90821008,
          0.90379286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          66,
          67,
          68,
          69,
          71
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "团队集思广益后，为“Sea Tea”取了新名字：Bichabi-cha。它结合了日语 cha（茶）与 bichabicha（湿漉漉、湿透了），同时有意模仿 Sōkenbicha（爽健美茶）等现实茶饮品牌。因此，日文名的文字游戏比英文原名的简单押韵又多了一层。",
        "status": "draft",
